DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251016
SUMMARY:Federal: 709 extended due date
DESCRIPTION:Extended due date\, via Automatic with a 1040 extension\, or Fo
 rm 8892 if not extending the income tax return. | Form 709 for 2025 gifts i
 s due April 15\, 2026. An extension of the donor's 2025 Form 1040 automatic
 ally extends the Form 709 due date\; if the income tax return is not being 
 extended\, Form 8892 requests a separate automatic 6-month extension. Exten
 sions to file do not extend the deadline to pay any gift or GST tax due. | 
 Authority: IRS Instructions for Form 709: "Generally\, you must file Form 7
 09 no earlier than January 1\, but not later than April 15\, of the year af
 ter the gift was made." | Source: https://www.irs.gov/instructions/i709 | T
 his date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-ann
 ounced change\; confirm against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
